  "content": "[Intro]\n[A#dim]\n[F5]\n[D#dim]\n\n[Bridge]\nI\n\n[Verse 1]\n[F5]try to assert myself\nI\nseek to dominate\nThe\nend justifies the means\nI\nwill be merciless\nI\n[A5]hold the ability to\ndestroy I\nhave the power to kill\nThe\nend justifies the means\nI will de-\nsign some disease\n\n[Bridge]\n[Adim]\n[A#dim]\n[Fdim]\n\n[Interlude]\n[Fdim]\n\n[Verse 2]\n[Fdim]What's a nation, what's\na continent?\nWhat's a fellow,\nwhat is a people?\n\n[Bridge]\n[Fdim]\n\n[Interlude]\n[Fdim]What is ethics, what's\nmorality?\nWhat's altruism,\nwhat's humanisem?\n\n[Bridge]\n[F5]\nNo-\nthing but sterile thoughts\n\n[Verse 3]\n[F5]There's no to stru-\ngigle\nNo resis-\ntance\nNo guerril-\nlas\nJust illu-\nsions\n\n[Verse 4]\n[C5]There's no peace\nNo negotiation\nNo mediation\nJust a hidden genocide\n\n[Bridge]\n[B5]\n[G#5]\nThis\n\n[Verse 5]\n[F#5]underdevel continent\nDe-\nserved only one thing\nTo\ndie in despicable ways\nAnd leave me its wealth\nI-\nmagine a virus\nAnd\npeople degenerating\nOver\nthree generations depths\nI-\nmagine a virus\n[Fdim]\n\n[Bridge]\n\n[Solo 1]\n[D5]\n[C#5]\n[D5]\n[G5]\n[D5]\n[A#5]\n[G5]\n[A5]\n[G5]\n[D5]\n[A#5]\n[F5]\n\n[Solo 2]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n[D5]  [D#5]  [D5]\n\n[Verse 6]\n[D5]  [A#5]\n[Edim]Crude phy-\nsicalic and mental\nalterations\n[D5]  [A#5/F]\nYour behavior dete-\nriorating [A5/E]\nYour instincts\n[D5]more debase [A#5]\n[Edim]Your\neating habits changing\nYou will fading out\n[D5]  [A#5/F]\nAll that makes you human\ndisappearing [A5/E]\nYou are turning\ninto a [G#5/D#]pig\n\n[Interlude]\n[G#5]  [G#5/D#]\n[D5]\n\n[Bridge]\n[G#5]\n[G5]\n[G#5]\n\n[Verse 7]\n[G5]Your face's\nshaping\nyour background\nTo gorge your are\nself and laze around\nSuce are your\nmotivations\n\n[Verse 8]\n[D5]Man's caricature,\neven your pride gets\n[F5]lost In the gaping bodies\nof your ripped open\n\n[Outro]\n[A#dim]\n[Bm6/D]\n[Am6/C]\n[Dm6/B]\n[Am6/C]\n[Bm6/F]\n[Am6/C]\n[G#7]\n[Bm6/F]\n[G7]\n[Bm6/F]\n[Am6/C]\n[G#7]\n[Cm6/D#]\n[Am6/C]\n[Dm6/B]\n[Am6/C]\n[Bm6/F]\n[Am6/C]\n[G#7]\n[Bm6/F]\n[G7]\n[Bm6/F]\n[Am6/C]\n[G#7]\n[Cm6/D#]",
